--- a/README
+++ b/README
@@ -20,6 +20,19 @@
 	make test
 	make install
 
+XPERL COMPATIBILITY
+
+On XPerl builds with PERL_RC_STACK, custom opcode handlers use
+XSPP_wrapped for their argument and result ownership. Alias descriptors
+use real SVs: integers for tags and indices, and references for containers
+and keys. Wrapping a handler alone cannot make raw pointer tags safe on a
+reference-counted stack.
+
+Handlers that call core opcodes or unwind scopes use the counted-stack
+APIs directly. Scope exits preserve aliases with leave_adjust_stacks in
+lvalue mode, and copy() uses rpp_is_lone to account for stack ownership.
+These changes are conditional on XPERL_VERSION and PERL_RC_STACK.
+
